# E0034: name defined twice

Functions and classes share one namespace, and so do the fields and methods of a class. Each name is defined once in its namespace. `print` is built in, so no function or class can take it.

## Why

A call or a type that names a duplicate could mean either definition. Sisu keeps the first and reports the second.

## Broken

```sisu
fn double(n: i64) -> i64 {
    n * 2
}

fn double(n: i64) -> i64 {
    n + n
}

fn main() {
    print(double(2))
}
```

## Fixed

```sisu
fn double(n: i64) -> i64 {
    n * 2
}

fn main() {
    print(double(2))
}
```
